# Rails — Rail R/U Manifestation Contract

> **Standing-harness rule.** Every merged ticket must leave evidence that the
> change actually manifested — a measurable delta (Rail R) or a user-facing
> surface (Rail U). The contract is intentionally cheap (one PR-body line) and
> fail-soft (the ledger never blocks a merge). Governed by `RAILS_LEDGER` in
> `.dev-context/project.conf`.

## The contract

**Every merged ticket declares one — and only one — Rail evidence line in its
PR body**, in this exact form:

```
Rail evidence: R — <one-line measurable claim>
Rail evidence: U — <one-line claim>
```

- **Rail R** ("Reasoning / measurable delta") — the change produced a
  measurable, ideally numeric, effect: a latency delta, a count, an
  xfail→pass, a FAIL→PASS demo, a ledger that did not exist before.
- **Rail U** ("UI / surface") — the change manifests on a user-facing surface:
  a rendered page, a screenshot-verified widget, a new visible output path.

The line is parsed by the strict regex `^Rail evidence: ([RU]) [—-] (.+)$`
(`scripts/rails.py::parse_rail_evidence`): uppercase `R`/`U` only, em-dash
(`—`) or hyphen (`-`), non-empty claim. A claim carrying a digit is recorded
`measurable=true`. A Markdown heading form (`## Rail evidence` followed by the
`R/U — claim` line) is also accepted.

## Enforcement points

| Surface | Behavior |
|---|---|
| `/develop` + `/sprint` agent prompt | The PR-body result schema **requires** the `Rail evidence:` field. |
| `/sprint merge` | Calls `rails.parse_and_append(...)` per PR. A body with **no valid line is flagged** (surfaced to the human; evidence-less tickets escalate) — the row is not written. Valid lines append to `kpis/rails.csv`. **Fail-soft**: a ledger I/O error never blocks the merge. |
| `/debrief` | Reports a **Rails coverage** KPI per wave + iteration: coverage % (tickets-with-claim / merged), R/U split, and count of measurable-R deltas. |

## Ledger

`.dev-context/kpis/rails.csv` — append-only, schema
`timestamp_utc,ticket,pr,rail,claim,measurable`. Pre-existing PRs are **not**
backfilled; measurement starts when the rule is adopted.

## Escalation

A merged ticket that genuinely has no R or U manifestation (pure internal
refactor with no observable delta) is not a silent skip — it is a signal
worth a human conversation: either the change lacked value, or the manifestation
was not captured. Flag it; do not invent evidence to satisfy the regex.
